ument — is squash-merged into the default branch once you finish. Your job in this session is to document what was actually implemented, so that[10;3Hsomeone meeting this part of the product later understands it without reading the diff.[12;3HSTEP 1 — Find out what was built. Read [38;2;177;185;249mplays/009-select-stop/intent.md [38;2;255;255;255mand [38;2;177;185;249mplays/009-select-stop/plan.md[38;2;255;255;255m, then read the real changes on the [38;2;177;185;249m009-select-stop [38;2;255;255;255mbranch of the [13;3Hproject's repositories ([38;2;177;185;249mgit log [38;2;255;255;255mand [38;2;177;185;249mgit diff [38;2;255;255;255magainst the default branch it was cut from). Where the plan and the code disagree, the CODE is the truth — the plan is only what was[14;3Hintended.[16;3HSTEP 2 — Find where it belongs. List [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/ [38;2;255;255;255mand read what is already there.[17;3H- If a document there ALREADY covers this play, UPDATE it. Do not add a second document about the same thing.[18;3H- Otherwise place a new document, respecting the granularity that already exists. If there are module folders, they are this product's modules: put the document in the one this [19;3Hplay belongs to, and only create a new module folder if this play genuinely is a new part of the product. If the documents are flat, keep them flat.[20;3H- If [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/ [38;2;255;255;255mis EMPTY, you are choosing the structure. Judge the size of the product from the vision, the tech stack and the repositories, then pick a granularity[21;3Hyou would still be happy with after twenty more plays: a small product is served well by a few flat documents, a larger one by a handful of module folders. Say in one line why [22;3Hyou chose what you chose.[23;3H- DEPTH LIMIT: only [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/<name>.md [38;2;255;255;255mor [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/<module>/<name>.md [38;2;255;255;255mare possible. There is no third level — do not try to nest deeper.[25;3HSTEP 3 — Write it. Describe the PRODUCT, not the changeset: what this part does, how it behaves, the decisions and constraints worth knowing, and anything a future implementer [26;3Hwould trip over. No changelog, no diff, no "we changed X to Y", no restating the intent. Keep it concise and concrete. Do not commit — Building commits your document on the [27;3Hplay's branch once you finish. Then end your turn with a short statement of what you wrote and where — not a question.[29;3HPROJECT CONTEXT FILES: this project keeps its documentation under [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/[38;2;255;255;255m; the documents in [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/ [38;2;255;255;255mare shared by every play and apply to all work. Read [30;3HALL of them before doing anything and make your work conform to them: [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/vision.md [38;2;255;255;255m(the problem, users, and product direction), [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/tech.md [38;2;255;255;255m[31;3H(overall architecture plus the technology used in each repository). Only the Architect writes [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/vision.md [38;2;255;255;255mand [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/tech.md[38;2;255;255;255m; treat every [32;3Hother document as read-only reference the user maintains, and do not create, move or edit anything under [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/ [38;2;255;255;255mEXCEPT [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/[38;2;255;255;255m, which is yours to write in[33;3Hthis session.[38;2;171;43;63m[49m[44;3HCoalescing… [38;2;153;153;153m(4[1Cs)[K[47;3H[?25h[m[?2026h[?2026l[?25l[38;2;193;81;75m[44;1H*[1CCoalescing… [38;2;153;153;153m[4C · thinking with high effort)[47;3H[?25h[m[?2026h[?2026l[?25l[38;2;199;91;78m[44;1H✶[1CCoalescing… [47;3H[?25h[m]0;◑ 009-select-stop implementation[?2026h[?2026l[?25l[38;2;199;91;78m[44;1H